dbr:Blood_Beach a dbo:Film ;
    rdfs:label "Blood Beach"@en ;
    dbo:abstract "Blood Beach is a 1981 American horror film written and directed by Jeffrey Bloom and starring David Huffman, John Saxon, and Burt Young. The premise, conceived by Steven Nalevansky, involves a creature lurking beneath the sand of Santa Monica Beach that attacks locals and vacationers. The film's tagline is: \"Just when you thought it was safe to go back in the water—you can't get to it.\""@en ;
    dbo:country "United States" ;
    dbo:director "http://dbpedia.org/resource/Jeffrey_Bloom" ;
