dbr:Blues_Brothers_2000 a dbo:Film ;
    rdfs:label "Blues Brothers 2000"@en ;
    dbo:abstract "Blues Brothers 2000 is a 1998 American musical comedy film directed by John Landis from a screenplay written by Landis and Dan Aykroyd, both of whom were also producers. The film, starring Aykroyd and John Goodman, is a sequel to the 1980 film The Blues Brothers. It also includes cameo appearances by various musicians. Blues Brothers 2000 was released on February 6, 1998 to mixed-to-negative reviews from critics and grossed $32.1 million on a budget of $30 million. Blues Brothers 2000 is dedicated to John Belushi, Cab Calloway and John Candy, cast members from the original film who had died prior to the sequel's production, in addition to Junior Wells, who died one month before it was released."@en ;
    dbo:country "United States" ;
