dbr:Goodbye_Lover a dbo:Film ;
    rdfs:label "Goodbye Lover"@en ;
    dbo:abstract "Goodbye Lover is a 1998 neo-noir comedy film about a murder plot surrounding an alcoholic advertising agency worker and his adulterous wife. The film was directed by Roland Joffé, and stars Patricia Arquette, Dermot Mulroney, Don Johnson, Ellen DeGeneres and Mary-Louise Parker. The original script was written by Ron Peer; subsequent drafts were written by Robert Pucci, then Buck Henry. The film premiered at the 1998 Cannes Film Festival, before being released theatrically in April 1999. Following its premiere, reshoots were done in Beverly Hills, and the climax was changed. This was the last film that Regency Enterprises had teamed up with Warner Bros. before teaming up with 20th Century Fox. until Warner Bros. Pictures released the 2006 romantic-fantasy drama movie The Fountain and only to be released by it."@en ;
    dbo:country "United States" ;
