dbr:Pushing_Tin a dbo:Film ;
    rdfs:label "Pushing Tin"@en ;
    dbo:abstract "Pushing Tin is a 1999 American comedy-drama film directed by Mike Newell. It centers on Nick Falzone (John Cusack), a cocky air traffic controller who quarrels over proving \"who's more of a man\" with fellow employee Russell Bell (Billy Bob Thornton). The film is loosely based around the real world New York TRACON radar facility. The film was a box office failure and received mixed reviews. The original music score was composed by Anne Dudley and Chris Seefried."@en ;
