dbr:Sixteen_Candles a dbo:Film ;
    rdfs:label "Sixteen Candles"@en ;
    dbo:abstract "Sixteen Candles is a 1984 American coming-of-age comedy film starring Molly Ringwald, Michael Schoeffling, and Anthony Michael Hall. Written and directed by John Hughes in his directorial debut, it was the first in a string of films Hughes would direct centering on teenage life. The film was a box office success, earning $23.6 million against a $6.5 million budget, and launched Ringwald to fame."@en ;
