dbr:What_About_Bob%3F a dbo:Film ;
    rdfs:label "What About Bob?"@en ;
    dbo:abstract "What About Bob? is a 1991 American black comedy film directed by Frank Oz and starring Bill Murray and Richard Dreyfuss. Murray plays Bob Wiley, a troubled patient who follows his self-centered psychotherapist Dr. Leo Marvin (Dreyfuss) on vacation. When Bob befriends the other members of Leo's family, the patient's problems push the doctor over the edge. The film received positive reviews and was a box office success. This film is number 43 on Bravo's \"100 Funniest Movies\"."@en ;
