dbr:You_Can_Count_on_Me a dbo:Film ;
    rdfs:label "You Can Count on Me"@en ;
    dbo:abstract "You Can Count on Me is a 2000 American drama film written and directed by Kenneth Lonergan (in his directorial debut) and starring Laura Linney, Mark Ruffalo, Rory Culkin, and Matthew Broderick. It tells the story of Sammy, a single mother living in a small Catskill Mountains town, and her complicated relationships with family and friends. The film and its performances received highly positive reviews among critics, and dozens of award nominations and awards at film festivals and during awards season. At the 73rd Academy Awards, the film received a nomination for Best Actress for Linney and a nomination for Best Original Screenplay for Lonergan."@en ;
    dbo:country "United States" ;
    dbo:director "http://dbpedia.org/resource/Kenneth_Lonergan" ;
